# What a fresh clone has to contain
# ---------------------------------
# A clone of this repo must open in Unity 6000.1.15f1 and build without anyone
# fetching anything by hand. That means these are TRACKED and must stay so:
#
#   UnitySim/Assets/            every asset AND its .meta — a missing .meta means
#                               Unity mints a new GUID on the other machine and
#                               every reference to that asset silently breaks
#   UnitySim/Packages/          manifest.json + packages-lock.json; the lock file
#                               pins exact package versions (Splines, Terrain
#                               Tools, ProBuilder), so the clone resolves to the
#                               same packages rather than the newest ones
#   UnitySim/ProjectSettings/   including ProjectVersion.txt (the editor version)
#                               and EditorBuildSettings.asset (the scene list)
#   Controllers/, UserScripts/, Blender/, Tools/, Docs/, Opus_Car_Spec/
#                               UserScripts ships the starter controller and its
#                               guide; a clone with an empty one has nothing to
#                               press "Build & Reload" on
#
# Everything ignored below is either regenerated by Unity on first open, or
# rebuilt by a script in this repo. Nothing here is a source file.

# ---- Unity: regenerated on first open ----
UnitySim/[Ll]ibrary/
UnitySim/[Tt]emp/
UnitySim/[Oo]bj/
UnitySim/[Bb]uild/
UnitySim/[Bb]uilds/
UnitySim/[Ll]ogs/
UnitySim/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
UnitySim/[Mm]emoryCaptures/
UnitySim/[Rr]ecordings/
UnitySim/[Aa]rtifacts/
UnitySim/[Bb]urst*/
UnitySim/sysinfo.txt
UnitySim/*.unitypackage

# Never ignore a .meta. Listed last-word here so a future pattern above cannot
# swallow one by accident — that failure is silent and expensive.
!*.meta

# Generated IDE/project files
*.csproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.opendb
*.VC.db
.vs/
.idea/
.vsconfig

# Built native plugin binaries — rebuild with Controllers/build.ps1.
# Their .meta files go too: NativeControllerLoader loads these through
# LoadLibrary/GetProcAddress by FILE NAME, not as a Unity asset reference, so a
# regenerated GUID breaks nothing and a .meta with no .dll beside it would just
# be deleted by the editor on the next import.
UnitySim/Assets/Plugins/x86_64/*.dll
UnitySim/Assets/Plugins/x86_64/*.dll.meta
UnitySim/Assets/Plugins/x86_64/*.pdb

# Asset Studio preview staging — copies of Blender exports made only so Unity
# has something to render before anyone has decided to commit them. Scratch by
# construction: the file of record is the export folder, the commit pipeline
# copies from THERE, and "Clear preview staging" empties this. Committing a
# staged copy would put a second, silently diverging original in the repo.
UnitySim/Assets/TinyTorqueAssets/AssetStudio/Staging/
UnitySim/Assets/TinyTorqueAssets/AssetStudio/Staging.meta

# Asset Studio slot-order scratch — an export imported WITH its materials for
# exactly as long as it takes to read which one sits in which submesh slot, then
# deleted in a finally. It should never survive a call, let alone reach a commit;
# this is here for the run that dies between the copy and the delete.
UnitySim/Assets/TinyTorqueAssets/AssetStudio/SlotProbe/
UnitySim/Assets/TinyTorqueAssets/AssetStudio/SlotProbe.meta

# Runtime output / personal data (settings, profiles, session snapshots)
UnitySim/TelemetryLogs/
UnitySim/Saves/

# Installer output (compiled by Inno Setup from UnitySim/Installer/*.iss)
UnitySim/Installer/Output/

# ---- Native controller build ----
Controllers/build/

# A compiler unpacked beside the game (see build.ps1). Redistributable, but a
# gigabyte of it, and never a source file in this repo.
Toolchain/

# ---- Blender authoring artifacts (source .blend + .py stay tracked) ----
Blender/*.blend1
Blender/*.fbx.bak*
Blender/renders/

# ---- Local logs / reports at repo root ----
# Anchored to the root: an unanchored *.log would also hide a log file committed
# deliberately anywhere else in the tree.
/*.log
/usage-report.html

# ---- Tooling ----
.claude/

# Scratch folder the JGraph bridge watches (figures exported from Tools/*.html)
Tools/jgraph-out/

# ---- Scratch scenes ----
# Scenes that exist to try something once. None is in EditorBuildSettings, none
# is named by a script, and none is a test fixture: the PhysicsTests, FlightTests
# and ModeTemplates scenes stay TRACKED, because [PHYS], [AERO] and [TPL] open
# them by path and a clone without them cannot run the suite.
#
# Two patterns rather than a folder, because scratch appears wherever the work
# is. Each needs its .meta listed too — the blanket "!*.meta" above would
# otherwise re-include it, and a .meta with no scene beside it is just a file
# Unity deletes on the next import.
*_Test_Scene.unity
*_Test_Scene.unity.meta
*_Backup.unity
*_Backup.unity.meta

# Asset Studio drafts — the in-progress edit state behind the Studio window, one
# ScriptableObject per key, recreated by AssetStudioDrafts.Find the moment anyone
# opens a row. Sibling of the Staging/ and SlotProbe/ rules above: the committed
# artifacts are the manifest and the asset, and a draft is what someone was
# thinking before they wrote one. Committing it would push a half-decided scale
# correction onto the next person's screen.
UnitySim/Assets/TinyTorqueAssets/AssetStudio/Drafts/
UnitySim/Assets/TinyTorqueAssets/AssetStudio/Drafts.meta

# ---- Per-user editor tool preferences ----
# ProjectSettings/ is tracked on purpose (see the header) — ProjectVersion.txt
# and EditorBuildSettings.asset are what make a clone build. This one file is
# not that: it is ProBuilder's own tool state — extrude distance, backface
# select, whether an edge loop grows iteratively. It records how somebody likes
# to model, changes on nearly every ProBuilder session, and affects no build
# output. ProBuilder recreates it with defaults on first use.
UnitySim/ProjectSettings/Packages/com.unity.probuilder/Settings.json

# ---- OS ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
